fihrist:manuscript_26523 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 1004" ;
    dct:description """This first of four incomplete volumes of the Razmnāmah (Book of Battles) a Persian translation of
                            the Mahābhārata , contains the first three Parva . Translated at the behest of the Mughal
                            ruler Akbar I (b. 1542, r. 1566–1605) starting in 990 AH
                                (1582–83 CE) by four scholars, chiefly Ibn ʿAbd al-Laṭīf Ḥusaynī Naqīb-K̲h̲ān (d. ca.
                                1614) , as well as ʻAbd
                                al-Qādir Badāʼūnī (ca. 1540–1615) , Muḥammad Sulṭān Thānīsārī fl. late 16th
                                c , and Mullā S̲h̲īrī (d. ca. 1586) ,
                            to which the vizier Abū al-Faz̤l
                                (1551–1602) added a preface. One of two sets of this work
                            previously held in the Chetham Library, Manchester.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_26523" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
