fihrist:manuscript_26556 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 956" ;
    dct:description """An undated, complete abridgement of a Persian treatise entitled Riyāz̤ al-Maẕāhib (Garden of
                            Religions), by Panḍit Māthurā Nāth Brahman Mālvī ,
                            Librarian of the Hindu College at Benares (Varanasi). Originally
                            composed in 1228 AH (1812
                                CE) . In his introduction, he describes how John
                                Glynn , then Benares City Registrar, inspired him to
                            prepare a survey of Indian religions. However, since the author of this
                            volume explicitly mentions both William
                                Augustus Brooke (1784–1833) , who long lived and ultimated
                            died in Benares, as well as William Wilberforce
                                Bird (1784-1857) , appointed Judge and Magistrate of
                            Benares in 1814, then promoted to Commissioner, 1826–1829. Therefore,
                            the completion of this abridgment likely dates to the latter's
                            tenure.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_26556" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Benares (Varanasi)" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_26556_person_22161693743415930845_cataloguer,
