fihrist:manuscript_26573 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 973" ;
    dct:date "1645-08-16" ;
    dct:description """The second part of the first volume of the Ḥabīb al-Siyar (Beloved of Biographies), uniformly bound with Persian
                           MS 974 , and probably intended to compliment and complete Persian MS 272 . Originally completed by author Ghiyās̲ al-Dīn ibn Humām al-Dīn (ca.
                        1475–1535) known as Khvāndamīr (1487–1524 CE) ,
                     in 937 AH (1530–31 CE) . He presents a general history spanning the
                     pre-Islamic period until the reign of Shāh Ismāʿīl I, which dedicates to
                     then-governor of Herat, Karīm al-Din
                        Khvājah Ḥabīb-Allāh Sāvajī (fl. early-mid 16th c.) , hence the
                     title. The entire work consists of a preface, an introduction, three
                     volumes—each of which contains four sections appended with lists of names of
                     prominent figures associated with each period—followed by an epilogue. This
                     volume covers the early Islamic period up to the medieval Khwarazm empire. An
                     unidentified scribe completed this volume on 22 Jumādá II 1055 AH (16 Aug. 1645 CE) during the
                     reign of Safavid ruler ShāhʿAbbās II. .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_26573" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Greater Iran" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
