fihrist:manuscript_6634 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 153" ;
    dct:date "late 18th to early 19th century CE." ;
    dct:description """The fourth of four volumes of the Siyar al-Mutaʼakhkhirīn (Review of Modern Times), with Persian MS 150 , an unrelated volume added to complete the set, but uniform with 151 , and 152 .
                     The author, Ghulām Husain Khān Ṭabaṭāḅāī (b. 1727 or 8) , a son of Patna Vice-Regent Sayyid ‘Alī Khān and cousin of ‘Alīvardī Khān, Nawwab of Bengal (b. 1676 r. 1740–1756) , composed this text in circa 1780–1784 , and dedicated it to Governor-General of Bengal, Warren Hastings .
                     A general history of India , it spans the death of the Mughal Emperor ‘Alamgīr I in 1707 until 1195 AH (1781 CE) .
                     Since the author relates many eyewitness accounts, historians regard it as a preeminent 18th-century source..
                     This volume ends at 20 Muḥarram 1195 AH (16 January 1781 CE) .""" ;
