fihrist:manuscript_6647 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 165" ;
    dct:description """An isolated second volume of the Ḥabīb al-Siyar (Beloved
                     of Biographies), originally completed in 937 AH (1530–1531 CE) by Ghiyās̲ al-Dīn ibn Humām al-Dīn (ca.
                        1475–1535) known as Khvāndamīr (1487–1524 CE) ,
                     a maternal grandson of Timurid-era historian Mīrkhvānd
                        (1433–1498) . A popular general history covering the pre-Islamic
                     period up to the reign of Shāh Ismāʿīl I, he dedicated it to then-governor of
                     Herat, Karīm al-Din Khvājah Ḥabīb-Allāh Sāvajī (fl. early-mid 16th
                        c.) , hence the title. The entire work consists of a preface, an introduction,
                     followed by three volumes, containing four sections each appended with lists of
                     names of prominent figures associated with specific periods, followed by an
                     epilogue. This volume covers the early Islamic period up until the reign of the
                     last Khwarazmshāh Jalāl al-Dīn Mingburnu (r. 1220–1231) .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_6647" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
