fihrist:manuscript_6678 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 199" ;
    dct:date "1775-07-28" ;
    dct:description """A copy of the Bahār-i Dānish (Spring of Wisdom) authored
                     by ʻInāyat
                        Allāh (d. ca. 1671) in 1061 AH (1651 CE) during the reign of Shāh Jahān , relates the romantic adventures of Jahāndār
                     Sulṭān and Bahravar Bānū, which serves as a frame story interwoven with other
                     tales. One of six copies held in the Rylands, this redaction contains a preface
                     by the author's younger brother and pupil Muḥammad Ṣāliḥ followed by the author's own introduction in
                     which he explains how he adapted the tale from one that he heard a young
                     Brahmin recite. A scribe named Muḥammad Ḥusayn Ghūrī Banī Hāshimī al-Qurayshī completed the
                     volume on behalf of Henry John Chandler (ca.
                        1754–1823) on 1189 AH (28 Jul. 1775 , who at that time served as a
                     Persian translator in Murshidabad, Bengal .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_6678" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Murshidabad" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
