fihrist:manuscript_6814 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 320" ;
    dct:date "before 1795" ;
    dct:description """An abridged selection of biographical notices of various nobles and statesmen culled from the Khizānah-ʼi ʻĀmirah (Royal Treasury), originally completed by the author, Ghulām ʻAlī ibn Nūḥ Āzād Bilgrāmī (1704–1786) in 1176 AH (1762–63 CE) . He completed it in Aurangabad , then the capital of the Hyderabad State very shortly after his close friend and patron, Niẓām al-Mulk ‘Alī Khān Āṣaf Jāh II (r. 1762–1803) , ascended the throne. 
                     A major Indian poet and author of several historical and biographical works, in this he relates the lives of some 135 Persian poets and recounts the Āsaf Jahi dynasty up to his patron and describes other elites, as well as the reigns of Aḥmad Shāh Durranī (r. 1747–1772) and the Maratha empire . 
                     Since he lived during many of these events and also relates vivid eyewitness accounts, historians deemed this work a reliable reference on 18th-century South Asia.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_6814" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Calcutta (Kolkata)" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_6814_person_120696480_fmo,
