fihrist:manuscript_6862 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 364" ;
    dct:date "1817-03-04" ;
    dct:description """A Persian treatise entitled Jām-i Jahān'numā-'i Sāsānī (The
                     World-Viewing Goblet of Sāsānī) bound together with the History of Shākmūnī or Gautama Buddha translated
                     from the Jamī‘ al-Tavārīkh (Compendium of Chronicles) of Rashīd
                     al-Dīn (d. 1318), the latter likely commissioned by John Staples Harriott , who once owned the Arabic manuscript now
