fihrist:manuscript_6961 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 465" ;
    dct:date "mid-17th century CE" ;
    dct:description """A rare collection of Inshā' (ornate prose)
                            correspondence primarily exchanged or received by the Deccan Sultanate
                            ruler Ibrāhīm Qutb Shah (b. 1518, r.
                                1550–1580) , with other rulers and elites. Compiled by one Muḥammad Qāsim
                                Tabasī , probably in the early 17th century ,
                            this undated and unsigned manuscript, probably completed in the Indian subcontinent , contains a seal impression dated regnal year ‘Ālamgīri 36 (1 Ramaz̤ān 1103–29 Sha‘bān 1104 AH / 17
                                May 1692–5 May 1693 CE) , so it may date relatively soon after
                            the work's completion.""" ;
