fihrist:manuscript_7304 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 798" ;
    dct:date "1634-05-09" ;
    dct:description """The first complete volume of the Akbarnāmah va Ā’īn-i
                        Akbarī (Book of Akbar and Akbar's Administration) by Abū
                        al-Faz̤l ibn Mubārak (1551–1602) , together with the second volume
                     by the same scribe, Persian MS
                           799 , to which a former owner added a third unrelated volume, Persian MS 800 , to complete and uniformly rebind as a
                     set. A Mughal courtier and ultimately Chief Secretary and close confidant of Akbar
                        (b. Akbar, b. 1542, r. 1556–1605) , the author relates vivid
                     accounts of events that occurred during his patron's reign, as well as a
                     concluding portion, known as the Ā’īn-i Akbarī (Akbar's
                     Administration) which features an extensive survey regarding various elites,
                     rivals, and cultural figures, regions, faiths, social groups, manufacturers,
                     and products within India at that time. A scribe named Mīr Ḥabīb Allāh valad-i Mīr ‘Ināyat Allāh
                        Astrābādī completed the first and second volumes, presumably in
                     the Indian
                        subcontinent , in 1043 AH (1634 CE) .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7304" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial """Indian
                        subcontinent""" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7304_person_22161693743415930845_cataloguer,
