    dct:description """The second volume of the Akbarnāmah va Ā’īn-i Akbarī (Book of Akbar and Akbar's Administration" by Abū al-Faz̤l ibn Mubārak (1551–1602), together with the first volume by the same scribe, Persian MS 798 , 
                     to which a former owner added a third unrelated volume, Persian MS 800 , to complete and uniformly rebind them as a set.
                     A Mughal courtier and ultimately Chief Secretary and close confidant of Akbar (b. Akbar, b. 1542, r. 1556–1605) , the author relates vivid accounts of events that occurred during his patron's reign, as well as a concluding portion, known as the Ā’īn-i Akbarī (Akbar's Administration) which features an extensive survey regarding various elites, rivals, and cultural figures, regions, faiths, social groups, manufacturers, and products within India at that time.
                     A scribe named Mīr Ḥabīb Allāh valad-i Mīr ‘Ināyat Allāh Astrābādī completed the first and second volumes, presumably in the Indian subcontinent , in 1043 AH (1634 CE) .""" ;
