fihrist:manuscript_7308 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 800" ;
    dct:description """The third and final volume of the Akbarnāmah va Ā’īn-i Akbarī (Book of Akbar and
                            Akbar's Administration" by Abū al-Faz̤l ibn Mubārak (1551–1602),
                            separately added by a former owner to the first two comparatively much
                            smaller volumes copied by another scribe, Persian MS 798 and Persian MS 799 , to complete and uniformly
                            rebind them as a set. A Mughal courtier and ultimately Chief Secretary
                            and close confidant of Akbar (b. Akbar, b. 1542, r.
                                1556–1605) , the author relates vivid accounts of events
                            that occurred during his patron's reign. This concluding portion, known
                            as the Ā’īn-i Akbarī (Akbar's Administration) which
                            features an extensive survey regarding various elites, rivals, and
                            cultural figures, regions, faiths, social groups, manufacturers, and
                            products within India at that time. This finely copied manuscript may
                            date to the 17th century, but it apparently never saw completion and
                            suffered subsequent damage. A later owner acquired and had the original
                            portion of the volume restored, with missing portions of the text
                            completed.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7308" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial """Indian
                                subcontinent""" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7308_person_22161693743415930845_cataloguer,
