fihrist:manuscript_7315 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 809" ;
    dct:date "1592" ;
    dct:description """The first of three volumes of the Ḥabīb al-Siyar (Beloved
                     of Biographies), uniformly bound with Persian MS
                        810 and 811 .
                     Originally completed in 937
                        AH (1530–1531 CE) by Ghiyās̲ al-Dīn ibn Humām al-Dīn (ca. 1475–1535) known as Khvāndamīr (1487–1524 CE) , a maternal grandson of Timurid-era
                     historian Mīrkhvānd (1433–1498) , he
                     presents a general history spanning the pre-Islamic period until the reign of
                     Shāh Ismāʿīl I, which dedicates to then-governor of Herat, Karīm al-Din Khvājah Ḥabīb-Allāh Sāvajī (fl. early-mid
                        16th c.) , hence the title. The entire work consists of a preface,
                     an introduction, followed by three volumes, containing four sections each
                     appended with lists of names of prominent figures associated with specific
                     periods, followed by an epilogue.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7315" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
