fihrist:manuscript_7327 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 82" ;
    dct:description "The first of two volumes of a Persian translation and commentary on the Qur‘ān entitled Mavāhib-i ʻAlīyah (Sublime Talents) or Tafsīr-i Ḥusaynī after its author, Ḥusayn Vāʻiẓ Kāshifī (d. ca. 1505 , who completed it between 1492 and 1494 . Evidently originally a very large single tome, a former owner split this manuscript into two volumes and had them uniformly rebound, together with Rylands Persian MS 195 ." ;
