fihrist:manuscript_7331 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 823" ;
    dct:date "1815-08-03" ;
    dct:description """Author Z̤iyāʼ al-Dīn Baranī (fl. 1284–1356) first
                     completed his Tārīkh-i Fīrūz Shāh (History of Fīrūz Shāh) when
                     74 years old in 758 AH (1357
                        CE) . From an prominent Delhi family, he personally knew influential
                     figures and poets including Amīr Khusraw and Ḥasan Dihlavī. Intended to
                     continue an earlier history of the Delhi Sultanate Ṭabaqāt-i Nāṣirī (Stages of Nāṣīr) completed by Minhāj
                        Sirāj Jūzjānī (1193–1266) in circa 1259–1260 CE, the work covers
                     the reigns of Balban to Fīrūz-S̲h̲āh’s sixth year, or nearly a century between
                     664–758 AH/1265–1357 CE. A scribe named Makhan La‘l completed this manuscript, which
                     contains many variant lines in comparison with others, Farrukhabad 26 Sha‘bān 1230 AH (3 Aug.
                        1815 CE) .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7331" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Farrukhabad" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
