fihrist:manuscript_7344 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 836" ;
    dct:date """45th regnal
                           year [‘Ālamgīrī 1112 AH] (1701–02 CE)""" ;
    dct:description """The second of two volumes, together with Persian MS
                           835 , of a Persian ornate prose paraphrased translation of
                     the Mahābhārata , completed by the Mughal poet Fayz̤ī (ca. 1547–1595) . He
                     derived his work in turn from an earlier literal translation entitled Ramznāmah completed by a team of four scholars to
                     which his younger brother, the Mughal minister Abū al-Faz̤l (1547–1595), added
                     a preface. A different unidentified Mughal-era scribe completed this volume
                     apart from the first by another hand, which contains the last twelve of
                     eighteen Parva , in 45th regnal
                     year , evidently that of Emperor ‘Ālamgīr I, or 1112 AH (1701–02 CE).""" ;
