fihrist:manuscript_7377 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 866" ;
    dct:date "1808-05-06" ;
    dct:description """Author Ḥubaysh ibn Ibrāhīm Tiflīsī (d. ca. 1203) dedicated this
                            comprehensive work on dream interpretation, here entitled Kitāb
                                al-Ta‘bīr fī Bayān al-Nawm va-al-Sir va-al-Z̤amīr (The Book
                            of Dream Interpretation on the Explanation of Sleep, Mystery, and
                            Thought) or more commonly as the Kāmil al-Ta‘bīr (Complete Book of Dream Interpretation) to his patron the Seljuq ruler
                            of the Sultanate of Rum, Sulṭān Qilij Arsalān b. Masʿūd (b. 1113 r.1156–1192) .
                            The work includes sixteen chapters with the last containing an
                            alphabetical list of over a thousand objects together with their
                            meanings. Completed by Sirāj al-Dīn
                                Māvarā' al-Nahrī on 8 Ẕī-al-Qa‘dah 808 AH (6 May 1406) ,
                            probably in the Timurid Empire , it is one of the earliest surviving
                            copies of this work known in the world today.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7377" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Timurid Empire" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7377_person_129280926_asn,
