fihrist:manuscript_7400 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 889" ;
    dct:date "1666-07-06" ;
    dct:description """Muṣṭafà Şem‘ī
                        (d. ca. 1602.) composed this Ottoman Turkish commentary on the
                     Persian Pandnāmah (Book of Advice),
                     spuriously ascribed to Farīd al-Dīn ʻAṭṭār . In his introduction, the author states how
                     his friend, Ṣāḥib al-Dawlah ʿÖmer bin Ḥüseyin requested that he complete the
                     work, which he dedicated to the latter’s patron Zeyrek Ağa, then presented it
                     to Sultan Murad III (b. 1546, r.
                        1574–1595 CE) when finished. The commentary itself consists of
                     verse by verse quotations, with their translations, and occasional glosses on
                     the original text, a style that the author maintains in his other Ottoman
                     commentaries on Persian works. An Ottoman-era scribe named Ahmet Kadır Bülevi completed this manuscript 3 Muḥarram 1077 AH (6 Jul. 1666
                        CE) .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7400" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial """Ottoman
                        empire""" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7400_person_120724759_dub,
